  "rootCause": "IDE receipt-backed input persisted clientMessageId/inputDigest in user_message, while its live conversation contained only role/content. Canonical completed-tool prefix comparison falsely reported SESSION_REVISION_STALE. Six real-adapter/headless offline cases reproduce before the fix, including Volcengine SSE configured like the report.",
  "changes": [
    "Normalize only those two top-level user receipt fields at conversation boundaries; retain exact original raw events, input receipt hashes and deduplication.",
    "Retain strict JSON validation and both live-prefix and locked-durable CAS comparisons; concurrent equal-content inputs with distinct receipts still fail stale.",
    "Normalize omitted OpenAI-compatible tool-response text to null.",
    "Settle completed tools before result retention, recompute the candidate after the host hook, propagate hook failure before another provider call, and preserve existing runtime-only capabilities on trusted clones.",
    "Authenticate historical raw and conversation lineage with separate exact source maps; summary parents must match one complete representation. Preserve legacy rewind/branch origins and raw branch digest authority.",
    "Recover interrupted physical imports only after exact raw snapshot and current conversation checks under the completion writer lock; preserve old completed migration digests.",
    "Align the release contract with all four child-package provenance gates."
  ],
